      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">This enzyme, which is found in bacteria and plants, is used to decompose cyanate, which can be used as the sole source of nitrogen [|CITS: [7768821][10801492]|. The reaction can be considered as the reverse of carbamate = cyanate + H2O&apos;, where this is assisted by reaction with bicarbonate and carbon dioxide |CITS: [3110153]|, and hence is classified in sub-subclass 4.2.1. Bicarbonate functions as a recycling substrate |CITS: [3110153]|.</Comment>
